  message: "DONE 2026-09-09. Record, instrument and pre-registration:\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/t0_sizing_09092026/fasoz/ (PLAN.md written before any\nnumber existed, typed_share.py, RESULT.md).\n\nANSWER: THE FIXTURE VERDICT HOLDS FOR JAVA, IS WEAK FOR SWIFT, AND IS REFUTED\nFOR SCALA.\n\n    lang    repo        ext. method edges   typed      %   rows reached (own edges)\n    java    killbill               53,482  34,762   65.0%     12 / 139\n    scala   sbt                    10,985       0    0.0%      0 / 164\n    scala   lila                   29,985       0    0.0%      0 / 164\n    swift   vapor                   3,067     505   16.5%     11 / 100\n\n\"typed\" = the module segment of an external method-call edge carries a real\nreceiver TYPE rather than the `external` sentinel. A method-kind row can only\nmatch when that slot holds the type (F3, INV-tapat/INV-maluk), so the typed\nshare is the CEILING on method-kind matching.\n\njava CONFIRMED, and above objc's 50.2% measured the same day. 12 rows reached\nthrough java's own edges: java.io.File.exists, java.io.FileWriter.write,\njava.net.http.HttpClient.send, five java.sql.ResultSet.get*. This cell now\nrests on behavioural corpus evidence rather than a fixture, which is what\nclosure-evidence discipline requires before INV-linub can be satisfied for it.\n\nscala REFUTED, categorically, on TWO independent repositories: 0 of 40,970\nexternal method-call edges carry a type. A 36 MB build tool and a 185 MB web\napplication. Boundary chains by edge language: sbt = bash 215 / java 35 / c 1 /\n**scala 0**; lila = typescript 255 / javascript 64 / bash 37 / python 31 /\n**scala 1**. Not a repo artifact -- scala emits all 40,970 method calls with\n`call_construct: \"method\"` and never types the receiver. Filed WI-sigog (P1);\n90% of scala's rows are at risk and it has no second disjunct.\n\nswift PASSES WEAKLY at 16.5%. The mechanism WORKS -- typed segments are real\ntypes (String, HTTPHeaders, ChannelHandlerContext, FileSystem, HTTPClient) --\nbut the untyped 83.5% are inferred and chained receivers (get 239, test 167,\ndecode 85, map 61). Same shape as WI-garar (objc), WI-dizag A (rust, closed),\nINV-mumov (python). Filed WI-dodop; 93 of swift's 107 rows are method-kind with\nno second disjunct.\n\nA MISATTRIBUTION THAT CHANGED TWO OF THE THREE NUMBERS, disclosed because it\nflattered: the first run credited scala with 14 reached method rows and java\nwith 16. `primitives_used` is a REPO-WIDE roll-up and java's and scala's\ncatalogues SHARE rows (`java.io.File.exists` is in both), so scala was being\ncredited with java's reach inside sbt, and java with JavaScript's inside\nkillbill. Attribution now comes from each chain's own `io_edge_dst` language\nprefix: scala 14 -> 0, java 16 -> 12, swift 11 -> 11. Swift did not move\nbecause vapor is single-language, which is exactly why a single-language repo\ncould not have exposed the bug. The loose count is retained in the JSON as\n`method_rows_reached_UNATTRIBUTED` so the size of the correction stays visible.\n\nBare-name matching was dropped in the same pass: sbt's reach set carries 50\nbare entries next to 20 qualified, among them shell command names and BINARY\ncontrol-character blobs plus an EMPTY STRING (filed WI-fisoh). Matching a\ncatalogue row's short name against that set is how `str.replace` becomes\n`Path.replace` -- the confusion F3 exists to prevent.\n\nWHY THE FIXTURE SAID OTHERWISE for scala is NOT diagnosed and is the first task\non WI-sigog. java was measured on the same instrument the same day at 65.0%, so\nthe instrument is not what produces the zero.\n\nOne repository per language, except scala where a categorical claim earned a\nsecond. This SIZES the cells; it does not certify the languages."  # 2353
